  "title": "Critical Stale Price Oracle Manipulation in Market Creation",
  "body": "## Summary\nThe protocol initializes new markets using a potentially stale oracle price. The createMarket function is non‑payable and does not update pull‑based oracles (e.g., Pyth) prior to reading the price inside LatentSwapLEX.initMarket. Meanwhile, user actions like mint/redeem/swap do update the oracle. This inconsistency allows attackers to initialize a market at an outdated price and immediately arbitrage once correct prices are refreshed, draining initial market liquidity.\n\n## Finding Description\n1) createMarket forwards directly to initMarket without any oracle price update:\n\nsrc/Covenant.sol (lines 211–228)\n```solidity\nfunction createMarket(\n    MarketParams calldata marketParams,\n    bytes calldata initData\n) external noDelegateCall returns (MarketId) {\n    // ...\n    (SynthTokens memory synthTokens, bytes memory lexData) = ILiquidExchangeModel(marketParams.lex).initMarket(\n        marketId,\n        marketParams,\n        _defaultProtocolFee,\n        initData\n    );\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n2) LatentSwapLEX.initMarket reads the price immediately; no _updateOraclePrice is called prior:\n\nsrc/lex/latentswap/LatentSwapLEX.sol (lines 246–256)\n\n```solidity\n// Read oracle (current market price) - revert on error\n(uint256 currentBasePrice, ) = LatentSwapLogic.readBasePriceAndCalculateLiqRatio(\n    marketParams,\n    _targetXvsL,\n    int8(info.quoteDecimals) - int8(info.synthDecimals),\n    false\n);\n```\n\n3) The price read uses getQuote (non‑preview) and depends on the oracle being fresh:\n\nsrc/lex/latentswap/libraries/LatentSwapLogic.sol (lines 1153–1187)\n\n```solidity\nfunction _readBasePriceAndCalculateLiqRatio(\n    MarketParams calldata marketParams,\n    uint256 targetXvsL,\n    int8 scaleDecimals,\n    bool isPreview\n) internal view returns (uint256 price, uint256 liqRatioX96) {\n    // ...\n    liqRatioX96 = (isPreview)\n        ? IPriceOracle(marketParams.curator).previewGetQuote(\n            scaledLiquidityConcentrationX96,\n            marketParams.baseToken,\n            marketParams.quoteToken\n        )\n        : liqRatioX96 = IPriceOracle(marketParams.curator).getQuote(\n            scaledLiquidityConcentrationX96,\n            marketParams.baseToken,\n            marketParams.quoteToken\n        );\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n4) All post‑creation user flows correctly update the oracle first (contrast):\n\n\n```solidity\nsrc/lex/latentswap/LatentSwapLEX.sol (lines 297–300)\n\nfunction mint(...) external payable onlyCovenantCore returns (...) {\n    // Update oracle price if necessary (external call and storage write)\n    _updateOraclePrice(mintParams.marketParams, mintParams.data);\n    // ...\n}\n\nsrc/lex/latentswap/LatentSwapLEX.sol (lines 338–341)\n\nfunction redeem(...) external payable onlyCovenantCore returns (...) {\n    _updateOraclePrice(redeemParams.marketParams, redeemParams.data);\n}\n\nsrc/lex/latentswap/LatentSwapLEX.sol (lines 377–379)\n\nfunction swap(...) external payable onlyCovenantCore returns (...) {\n    _updateOraclePrice(swapParams.marketParams, swapParams.data);\n}\n```\n\n\n5) Updating a pull‑based oracle is payable:\n\nsrc/interfaces/IPriceOracle.sol (lines 37–43)\n\n```solidity\n/// priceUpdate for pulled pricing (e.g., Pyth...)\nfunction updatePriceFeeds(address base, address quote, bytes calldata updateData) external payable;\n```\n\n6) The “smoking gun”: createMarket is non‑payable, so it cannot forward the oracle fee. Thus, it is impossible to safely call createMarket directly in pull‑oracle mode.\n\n7) The protocol’s multicall cannot fix this (only delegate‑calls into Covenant and forces strict balance equality):\n\n\n```solidity\nsrc/libraries/MultiCall.sol (lines 21–33)\n\nfunction multicall(bytes[] calldata data) internal returns (bytes[] memory results) {\n    results = new bytes[](data.length);\n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {\n        results[i] = Address.functionDelegateCall(address(this), data[i]);\n    }\n    return results;\n}\n\nsrc/Covenant.sol (lines 506–524)\n\nfunction multicall(bytes[] calldata data) external payable returns (bytes[] memory results) {\n    uint256 balanceBeforeCall = address(this).balance - msg.value;\n    _isMulticall = true;\n    results = MulticallLib.multicall(data);\n    _isMulticall = false;\n    if (address(this).balance != balanceBeforeCall) revert Errors.E_IncorrectPayment();\n    return results;\n}\n\n```\n\nBecause multicall delegate‑calls into Covenant itself, it cannot call an external oracle adapter’s updatePriceFeeds directly; and the strict balance check further constrains fee handling.\n\n## Impact Explanation\nSeverity: HIGH.\n\nWhy high:\n- Initialization sets LexState.lastBaseTokenPrice and derived invariants. If stale, the market is born mispriced.\n- An attacker can create a market when the oracle lags, then immediately perform mint/redeem/swap (which refreshes to the true price) to arbitrage the price gap established at initialization.\n- The non‑payable nature of createMarket mathematically prevents safe price updates through the direct path, proving this is a design flaw (not user error).\n\nConcrete exploit path:\n- Attacker monitors for stale oracle windows.\n- Calls createMarket (no fee, no update → stale price used).\n- Immediately invokes a state‑changing action (mint/redeem/swap), which updates to the correct price and unlocks a deterministic arbitrage of the mispricing.\n- Early LPs or bootstrap funds are directly impacted; loss can be catastrophic.\n\n## Likelihood Explanation\nHigh likelihood:\n- createMarket is the obvious, first entrypoint to spin up markets.\n- No natspec warnings instruct users to avoid direct use or to wrap with a safe helper.\n- Pull‑based oracles (e.g., Pyth) are common and require fees; createMarket cannot pass them.\n\n## Recommendation\n- Make market creation safe for pull‑based oracles:\n  - Option A: Make createMarket payable and forward msg.value (and initData) to an oracle update hook before any initial price read.\n  - Option B (preferred): In LatentSwapLEX.initMarket, call _updateOraclePrice before readBasePriceAndCalculateLiqRatio, using initData and msg.value passed through from createMarket."
